## 3. Safety obligations

### 3.1 S1 (signature lift)

Prove at **every call site** (private fn → module-wide grep; `pub` fn →
crate-wide grep):

1. Callers do not pass overlapping memory regions to two `&mut [T]`
   parameters in the same call.
2. Callers do not hold any other `&` / `&mut` reference to the same
   backing memory during the call.
3. The raw pointer was not null (needed for `slice::from_raw_parts_mut`).
4. `len` accurately reflected the buffer size at every call site.

